# Shell scripts are executed inside Linux containers and by systemd on the
# server. With core.autocrlf=true a Windows checkout gives them CRLF endings,
# the shebang becomes "#!/bin/sh\r", and the image fails at runtime with the
# unhelpful "exec /start.sh: no such file or directory". Pin them to LF so the
# checkout a developer builds from matches the one CI builds from.
*.sh text eol=lf

# Same reason: these are copied into images and run there.
Dockerfile* text eol=lf
*.Dockerfile text eol=lf
